I have analyzed the JSON representation of the "Registration procedure for initial registration" according to the 3GPP NAS specifications (TS 24.501) and found the following correctness issues:

✅ Correct Elements:
Initial State (5GMM-DEREGISTERED) – The UE starts in this state before sending a REGISTRATION REQUEST.

State Transition to 5GMM-REGISTERED-INITIATED – Correctly captured when UE sends REGISTRATION REQUEST.

Common Procedures Trigger – The AMF may initiate 5GMM common procedures before responding.

REGISTRATION ACCEPT and REGISTRATION COMPLETE – Properly included.

Handling of REGISTRATION REJECT – Included with the appropriate transition.

T3510 Timer Expiry – Mentioned correctly, leading to ATTEMPTING-REGISTRATION if the attempt counter <5.

❌ Issues Found:
Incorrect Transition for REGISTRATION ACCEPT:

The REGISTRATION ACCEPT should transition to 5GMM-REGISTERED-INITIATED before reaching 5GMM-REGISTERED.

The JSON directly transitions to 5GMM-REGISTERED, skipping the intermediate 5GMM-REGISTERED-INITIATED after receiving REGISTRATION ACCEPT.

REGISTRATION COMPLETE should be tied to Security Mode Procedure:

The SECURITY MODE COMMAND procedure usually happens before REGISTRATION COMPLETE.

This is not included in the flow, making the procedure incomplete.

5GMM-COMMON-PROCEDURE-INITIATED is not a defined NAS state:

The JSON introduces a "5GMM-COMMON-PROCEDURE-INITIATED" state, which is not explicitly defined in NAS specifications.

Common procedures (like authentication, security mode) occur within 5GMM-REGISTERED-INITIATED, but they don’t form a separate state.

REGISTRATION REJECT Handling Needs Improvement:

After REGISTRATION REJECT, the UE should go back to 5GMM-DEREGISTERED instead of a separate state "UE receives REGISTRATION REJECT".

Security Procedures Missing (Authentication & Security Mode Command):

The Authentication Procedure (Authentication Request/Response) is missing.

The Security Mode Command/Complete step is missing.

